---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { termsLastUpdated } from "../data/termsLastUpdated";
---
<!-- Load Base Layout -->
    <BaseLayout title="Terms of Service - RaccStarLogan" description="By commissioning me, you agree to the following Terms of Service. Please read them carefully.">
    <section class="hero">
        <h1>RaccStarLogan's Terms of Service and Content Usage Policy</h1>
        <p>By commissioning me, using my content, and creating fan works based on my work, you agree to the following Terms of Service.</p>
        {termsLastUpdated.sfw && (
            <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 0.95rem;">Last updated: {termsLastUpdated.sfw}</p>
        )}
    </section>

    <section class="article-section">
        <h1>1. General Terms</h1>
        <p>Unless otherwise agreed in writing, I retain full copyright ownership of all original work that I create.</p>
        <p>Purchasing a commission, recieving artwork, or otherwise obtaining my content does not transfer copyright ownership. Only the rights explicitly granted by these terms are provided.</p>
        <p>I reserve the right to pursue takedowns, revoke permissions, refuse future service, or take legal action where appropriate if I believe my work is being misused, redistributed without permission, or used in violation of these terms.</p>
        <p>I have the right to modify these terms at any time, with or without prior notice.</p>
        <p>These terms should be interpreted according to their intended purpose. Attempts to exploit technicalities, ambiguities, or perceived loopholes may be considered vviolation of these terms.</p>
        <h1>2. Artificial Intelligence &amp; Data Usage</h1>
        <p>Unless I have given explicit written permission beforehand:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>My artwork, writing, music, designs, characters, and other creative works may not be used to train artificial intelligence or machine learning systems.</li>
            <li>My content may not be used in datasets used for AI training or development.</li>
            <li>My content may not be scraped, harvested, archives, or collected for AI-related purposes.</li>
            <li>My content may not be used to develop, replicate, imitate, or generate works intended to mimic my style.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Permission for one use does not imply permission for any future use.</p>
        <p>Permission to view, download, purchase, or commission my work does not constitute permission for AI training or dataset inclusion.</p>
        <p>My work may not be minted, sold, distributed, or used in connection with NFTs, blockchain assets, or similar technologies.</p>
        <p>If you are uncertain whether a use falls under these restrictions, ask first.</p>
        <h1>3. Commission Terms</h1>
        <h2>3.1. Eligibility</h2>
        <p>All commission clients must be at least 18 years of age. No exceptions will be made.</p>
        <h2>3.2. Payment</h2>
        <p>All prices are listed in USD.</p>
        <p>Payment is generally required upfront unless another arrangement has been agreed upon beforehand.</p>
        <h2>3.3. Licensing</h2>
        <p>Commissioned artwork is licensed for personal use only unless otherwise agreed.</p>
        <p>Commercial usage rights and merchandising rights are not automatically included with commissions.</p>
        <p>Commercial licenses and merchandising licenses may be purchased separately, typically at an additional fee equivalent to the original commission price. Purchasing a commercial license does not transfer copyright ownership.</p>
        <p>Custom character designs are exempt from this restriction. Ownership and usage rights for commissioned character designs, excluding the artwork being commissioned, are automatically given to the client.</p>
        <h2>3.4. Rejection of Service</h2>
        <p>I reserve the right to refuse any commission inquiry for any reason and am not obligated to provide an explanation.</p>
        <p>I may also cancel a commission at any stage if:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The subject matter becomes uncomfortable for me.</li>
            <li>The client violates these terms.</li>
            <li>Communication becomes unreasonable or hostile.</li>
            <li>Information comes to light regarding the client's behavior or reputation that makes me undomfortable continuing the commission.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>3.5. Refunds &amp; Cancellations</h2>
        <p>Refunds are based on the ammount of work completed at the time of cancellation.</p>
        <p>As a general guideline:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>No work completed = Full refund</li>
            <li>Partial work completed = Partial refund</li>
            <li>Final production stage reached = No refund</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Audio commissions (music, voice-over, etc.) are non-refundable.</p>
        <p>If a commission is terminated due to a client's violation of these terms, harassment, misconduct, or other behavior that reasonably prevents me from completing the wor, refunds may be reduced or denied at my discretion.</p>
        <h1>4. Commission Content Guidelines</h1>
        <p>The following categories are generally accepted:</p>
        <p><strong>Will Do:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Original characters</li>
            <li>Fan characters</li>
            <li>Horror content</li>
            <li>NSFW content (subject to additional restrictions)</li>
            <li>Other subjects at my discretion</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Won't Do:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Hate speech</li>
            <li>Discriminatory content</li>
            <li>Illegal content</li>
            <li>Content that promotes harm toward others</li>
            <li>Content that I personally find inappropriate or uncomfortable</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This list is not exhaustive.</p>
        <p>I retain the right to refuse any request regardless of whether it appears on this list.</p>
        <h1>5. Posting, Credit &amp; Usage</h1>
        <p>Commissioned work may not be sold, redistributed, relicensed, or otherwise commercialized without obtaining the appropriate license.</p>
        <p>Unless otherwise requested, I reserve the right to publicly display commissioned work through:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Portfolios</li>
            <li>Social media</li>
            <li>Promotional materials</li>
            <li>Galleries</li>
            <li>Livestreams</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you would like a commission kept private, please discuss this before work begins.</p>
        <h2>Twitter / X</h2>
        <p>When posting my artwork to Twitter/X, my watermark must remain visible.</p>
        <p>If you intend to post commissioned work to Twitter/X, you may request a platform-specific export.</p>
        <p>Requests for versions without watermarks may incur an additional fee.</p>
        <h2>Artist Credit</h2>
        <p>Credit is required whenever reasonably possible.</p>
        <p>Where credit is provided, please credit me as <strong>"RaccStarLogan"</strong> unless otherwise specified.</p>
        <p>For all NSFW content, you must credit me as <strong>"Jesper Skulldragon"</strong> instead.</p>
        <h1>6. Enforcement</h1>
        <p>Violation of these terms may result in:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>License revocation</li>
            <li>Removal/Takedown requests</li>
            <li>Refusal of future service</li>
            <li>Blacklisting from future commissions</li>
            <li>Other actions deemed appropriate for the situation</li>
        </ul>
        <p>I reserve the right to distance myself from clients, projects, or uses of my work that I no longer wish to be associated with.</p>
        <h1>7. Mature Content Policy</h1>
        <p>NSFW commissions are subject to all standard commission terms in addition to the requirements below.</p>
        <p>I maintain a separate list of prohibited subject matter. This list may change over time. <a href="/nsfw/terms/additional">You may find the list here.</a></p>
        <p>All NSFW commissions are ineligable for merchandising or commercial licenses.</p>
        <h1>8. Fan Content Policy</h1>
        <p>Fan content based on my original works, characters, settings, and intellectual property is generally permitted and encouraged.</p>
        <p>This includes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Fanart</li>
            <li>Fanficiton</li>
            <li>Fan animations</li>
            <li>Memes</li>
            <li>Commentary and analysis</li>
            <li>Cosplay</li>
            <li>Other transformative fan works</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fan works, including NSFW works, are permistted provided they are not created with the intent to harass, harm, defame, or otherwise target an individual group.</p>
        <p>Additional restrictions may apply as outlined elsewhere within these terms.</p>
        <h1>9. REDRIFT Fan Work Policy</h1>
        <p>I generally encourage fan participation involving REDRIFT and related projects.</p>
        <p>Fanart, fanfiction, discussions, theories, animations, and other similar community projects are welcome.</p>
        <h2>Canon Policy</h2>
        <p>Characters on my <a href="https://reference.ink/u/raccstarlogan" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">reference.ink</a> page identified as fan characters, "DNA Lab Cousins," or similar fan-created additions are not canon to REDRIFT or any associated works unless explicitly stated otherwise.</p>
        <p>Likewise, my own personal commissions should not automatically be considered canon unless I specifically state they are.</p>
        <p>Unless explicitly stated otherwise, all fan works should be assumed to be non-canon.</p>
        <h2>Fan Merch</h2>
        <p>Mass-produced merchandise based on REDRIFT or any of my intellectual property is not permitted without permission.</p>
        <p>However, small-scale handmate merchandise sold at conventions, artist alleys, local events, or similar venues is generally acceptable.</p>
        <p>If you are interested in producing official merchandise or collaborating on merch production, please contact me directly.</p>
        <h2>Shipping &amp; Fan Interpratation</h2>
        <p>Shipping, kinning, yumeshipping, and other forms of fan engagement are generally acceptable.</p>
        <p>However:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Please maintain appropriate boundaries.</li>
            <li>These are my characters. I have the final say in what's canon.</li>
            <li>Do not ship my characters with real people other than myself.</li>
            <li>DO NOT END PERSONAL RELATIONSHIPS OVER A YUMESHIP.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Cross-media ships involving fictional characters from other works are acceptable.</p>
        <h2>FICTIONAL RELIGION DISCLAIMER</h2>
        <p>REDRIFT CONTAINS FICTIONAL RELIGIONS, PROPHECIES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND BELIEF SYSTEMS.</p>
        <p>THESE ELEMENTS ARE PURELY FICTIONAL AND NOT INTENDED AS REAL-WORLD IDEOLOGIES, GUIDANCE, RELIGIOUS INSTRUCTION, OR ORGANIZATIONAL MODELS.</p>
        <p>PLEASE DO NOT FORM REAL-WORLD CULTS, RELIGIONS, ORGANIZATIONS, OR MOVEMENTS BASED ON REDRIFT.</p>
        <p>SERIOUSLY. DON'T BE WEIRD. YOU WILL BE MADE FUN OF.</p>
        <h2>NSFW Restrictions.</h2>
        <p>The following restrictions apply to fan works involving my IP:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>All NSFW content involving Leo the Wickerbeast is strictly prohibited. This restriction is non-negotiable and applies regardless of platform, medium, or context.</li>
            <li>Incestuous ships (Logan x Jesper) are prohibited.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Additional character-specific restrictions may be added in the future if necessary.</p>
        <h1>10. Contact</h1>
        <p>Questions regarding these terms, licensing, merchandise rights, commercial usage, fan projects, or other concerns may be directed to me through my listed contact methods:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Discord (@racc.star.logan)</li>
            <li>Telegram (@RaccStarLogan)</li>
            <li>Stoat (@raccstarlogan#3020)</li>
            <li>Email (contact@raccstarlogan.com)</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
    <br />
</BaseLayout>
